1
00:00:06,589 --> 00:00:09,505
(liquid bubbling)

2
00:00:23,340 --> 00:00:25,590
Don't you poke around inside me.

3
00:00:25,673 --> 00:00:27,381
Not without my permission!

4
00:00:27,465 --> 00:00:29,256
I hate that, punk ass!

5
00:00:30,131 --> 00:00:31,215
Then you come down here

6
00:00:31,298 --> 00:00:33,548
and I'll tear you open!

7
00:00:34,673 --> 00:00:37,882
(opening theme music)

8
00:02:06,968 --> 00:02:08,885
"Episode 6: After Rain"

9
00:02:15,635 --> 00:02:17,718
You're being awfully
hostile, aren't you?

10
00:02:17,801 --> 00:02:18,718
Ha!

11
00:02:18,801 --> 00:02:19,927
You got that right!

12
00:02:20,009 --> 00:02:21,235
You expect kindness
after you murdered me?

13
00:02:21,259 --> 00:02:23,509
So that's the thanks I get

14
00:02:23,593 --> 00:02:25,551
for healing your arm and hand?

15
00:02:25,635 --> 00:02:27,343
Let's not forget
that right after that

16
00:02:27,426 --> 00:02:29,552
you ripped out my heart!

17
00:02:29,636 --> 00:02:32,385
Where are we
anyway, is this hell?

18
00:02:32,469 --> 00:02:35,177
I'm not crazy about being
stuck with you for eternity.

19
00:02:37,344 --> 00:02:39,177
But I'll make it work.

20
00:02:39,260 --> 00:02:40,260
And you'll pay!

21
00:02:44,844 --> 00:02:46,177
(charge yell)

22
00:02:46,260 --> 00:02:48,594
I hope you're ready for this!

23
00:02:58,552 --> 00:02:59,385
He was aiming for where I stood?

24
00:02:59,469 --> 00:03:01,219
You fell for it!

25
00:03:01,469 --> 00:03:03,220
Got you!

26
00:03:04,220 --> 00:03:05,929
What the?

27
00:03:06,011 --> 00:03:07,136
You're just so predictable.

28
00:03:07,220 --> 00:03:08,261
Ah!

29
00:03:11,220 --> 00:03:13,345
I was sure I'd landed
that one perfectly!

30
00:03:15,845 --> 00:03:16,762
Damn it.

31
00:03:16,845 --> 00:03:18,803
This isn't the afterlife.

32
00:03:18,887 --> 00:03:21,053
This place is my Innate Domain.

33
00:03:21,136 --> 00:03:22,929
Innate Domain?

34
00:03:23,011 --> 00:03:24,929
Fushiguro talked about!

35
00:03:25,011 --> 00:03:27,220
Or think of it as
being in my mind.

36
00:03:27,303 --> 00:03:30,261
In short, you could say
we're not dead just yet.

37
00:03:30,345 --> 00:03:31,261
Oh.

38
00:03:31,345 --> 00:03:32,446
If you'll accept my conditions,

39
00:03:32,470 --> 00:03:36,094
I'll fix your heart and
bring us both back to life.

40
00:03:36,178 --> 00:03:37,596
Cocky bastard.

41
00:03:37,679 --> 00:03:39,596
Don't act like you're
doing me a favor!

42
00:03:39,679 --> 00:03:41,596
I know you don't
want to die either!

43
00:03:41,679 --> 00:03:43,638
But the situation has changed.

44
00:03:43,721 --> 00:03:47,763
Very soon I'll be able to
see something interesting.

45
00:03:49,429 --> 00:03:51,179
I have just two conditions.

46
00:03:51,262 --> 00:03:53,304
Number one is whenever
I chant the word Extension,

47
00:03:53,387 --> 00:03:56,638
you'll surrender your
body to me for one minute.

48
00:03:56,721 --> 00:03:59,262
Two, you'll completely
forget you made this promise.

49
00:03:59,346 --> 00:04:00,262
No way!

50
00:04:00,346 --> 00:04:01,488
I don't know what
you're really after here

51
00:04:01,512 --> 00:04:03,471
but it's shady as hell.

52
00:04:03,554 --> 00:04:06,346
I finally get what
you're really about now.

53
00:04:06,429 --> 00:04:07,804
You are pure evil!

54
00:04:07,888 --> 00:04:10,639
And I'm not lending
you my body ever again!

55
00:04:10,722 --> 00:04:13,222
During that minute I
won't kill or injure anyone.

56
00:04:13,305 --> 00:04:15,805
Is that enough to
address your concerns?

57
00:04:16,388 --> 00:04:18,305
Loser.

58
00:04:18,388 --> 00:04:19,305
[Yuuji] Like I'd
ever believe you!

59
00:04:19,388 --> 00:04:23,013
It's not about whether
you believe me or not.

60
00:04:23,096 --> 00:04:24,305
This is a pact, a geas.

61
00:04:24,388 --> 00:04:27,347
I'll be the one
punished if I break it.

62
00:04:28,972 --> 00:04:31,138
(pain scream)

63
00:04:31,222 --> 00:04:33,222
And if you pursue selfish
gain beyond your means,

64
00:04:33,305 --> 00:04:36,138
you will suffer retribution.

65
00:04:36,222 --> 00:04:39,138
I'm certain you've
experienced that for yourself.

66
00:04:39,222 --> 00:04:40,281
It wasn't a problem before!

67
00:04:40,305 --> 00:04:41,222
Hm.

68
00:04:41,305 --> 00:04:42,347
Huh?

69
00:04:43,306 --> 00:04:46,681
Oh, you mean that time
I wanted to switch, too.

70
00:04:46,765 --> 00:04:49,556
And you were just doing
what that sorcerer told you to.

71
00:04:52,806 --> 00:04:55,723
A pact founded
in mutual interest.

72
00:04:55,806 --> 00:04:58,431
That's one of the key
factors behind all jujutsu.

73
00:05:00,014 --> 00:05:01,181
Fine, then.

74
00:05:01,264 --> 00:05:02,556
Get off of me already.

75
00:05:02,640 --> 00:05:03,760
I'll accept your conditions.

76
00:05:09,431 --> 00:05:11,848
I don't understand
exactly what you're up to,

77
00:05:13,014 --> 00:05:14,654
just that it means
I'll come back to life!

78
00:05:18,641 --> 00:05:19,933
I'd never accept that!

79
00:05:20,015 --> 00:05:22,557
Bring me back to life
without any conditions.

80
00:05:22,641 --> 00:05:25,515
It's all thanks to you I
died in the first place.

81
00:05:25,599 --> 00:05:28,182
Well how about this then?

82
00:05:28,265 --> 00:05:29,265
We'll fight to the death

83
00:05:29,349 --> 00:05:31,724
and I'll do it without
conditions if you defeat me.

84
00:05:31,807 --> 00:05:35,307
But if I win then you live
only under my two conditions.

85
00:05:35,390 --> 00:05:36,307
Yeah!

86
00:05:36,390 --> 00:05:37,682
I'll kick your ass for...

87
00:05:43,515 --> 00:05:47,766
[Gojou] You know, I have
a deeply flawed personality.

88
00:05:47,849 --> 00:05:48,766
[Ijichi] I know.

89
00:05:48,849 --> 00:05:49,432
Ijichi, expect a forehead flick.

90
00:05:49,515 --> 00:05:50,433
(gasp)

91
00:05:50,516 --> 00:05:52,975
A forehead flick?

92
00:05:53,058 --> 00:05:54,683
Being a teacher is not my style.

93
00:05:54,767 --> 00:05:56,558
Do you know why I
decided to become

94
00:05:56,642 --> 00:05:59,225
a teacher at this
school in the first place?

95
00:05:59,308 --> 00:06:00,308
Ask me.

96
00:06:00,391 --> 00:06:03,141
Why did you do it?

97
00:06:03,225 --> 00:06:04,934
Because I have a dream.

98
00:06:05,016 --> 00:06:06,934
[Ijichi] You have a dream?

99
00:06:07,016 --> 00:06:07,934
Yup.

100
00:06:08,016 --> 00:06:10,141
As you can see in
this case with Yuuji,

101
00:06:10,225 --> 00:06:13,225
the top of the jujutsu
world is a den of vice.

102
00:06:13,308 --> 00:06:16,516
Conservative fools,
traditional fools, arrogant fools,

103
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:18,391
just plain fools.

104
00:06:18,475 --> 00:06:20,600
It's a bargain sale
on rotten mikan!

105
00:06:20,683 --> 00:06:24,517
And I want to reset that
garbage jujutsu world.

106
00:06:26,893 --> 00:06:29,809
Murdering all the fools at
the top would be an easy task.

107
00:06:29,893 --> 00:06:31,493
But no fix, 'cause they'd
all just get replaced

108
00:06:31,517 --> 00:06:34,267
and there'd be no revolution.

109
00:06:34,351 --> 00:06:36,559
Plus if I did that, no one
would want to follow me.

110
00:06:39,059 --> 00:06:41,434
That's why I chose
education instead.

111
00:06:41,517 --> 00:06:44,726
As a way to raise up
strong, clever compatriots.

112
00:06:47,142 --> 00:06:48,434
And sometimes it's also

113
00:06:48,517 --> 00:06:50,976
why I send students
to do my missions.

114
00:06:51,059 --> 00:06:52,142
It's tough love.

115
00:06:52,226 --> 00:06:54,142
Or a chance for
you to slack off.

116
00:06:54,226 --> 00:06:55,434
And they're all talented.

117
00:06:55,517 --> 00:06:58,227
Especially Hakari,
the third-year,

118
00:06:58,310 --> 00:06:59,852
and the second-year, Okkotsu.

119
00:06:59,936 --> 00:07:02,393
They'll become jujutsu
sorcerers on a par with me.

120
00:07:02,477 --> 00:07:05,477
Yuuji would have been
one of them as well.

121
00:07:08,894 --> 00:07:09,894
Hey you two.

122
00:07:09,936 --> 00:07:10,518
-Hm?
-Hm?

123
00:07:10,602 --> 00:07:13,060
I'm going to get started.

124
00:07:13,143 --> 00:07:14,685
Are you gonna watch from there?

125
00:07:14,769 --> 00:07:17,101
(shock gasp)

126
00:07:17,185 --> 00:07:18,060
Hm?

127
00:07:18,143 --> 00:07:19,060
Whoa!

128
00:07:19,143 --> 00:07:20,060
Where're my clothes?!

129
00:07:20,143 --> 00:07:21,185
G-G-G-Gojou!

130
00:07:21,936 --> 00:07:22,852
He's alive!

131
00:07:22,936 --> 00:07:23,852
Are you seeing this?

132
00:07:23,936 --> 00:07:24,518
-He's alive!
-Ijichi stop.

133
00:07:24,602 --> 00:07:25,644
I'm a little bummed.

134
00:07:25,727 --> 00:07:27,685
Yeah, well.

135
00:07:27,769 --> 00:07:28,518
It's embarrassing
but, who are you?

136
00:07:28,602 --> 00:07:29,518
[Gojou] Hi, Yuuji!

137
00:07:29,602 --> 00:07:30,603
Huh?

138
00:07:31,603 --> 00:07:32,603
Welcome back!

139
00:07:35,144 --> 00:07:36,061
Yo!

140
00:07:36,144 --> 00:07:37,186
Well thanks.

141
00:07:42,978 --> 00:07:43,895
What a pain.

142
00:07:43,978 --> 00:07:46,144
I'm going to have to
revise all the reports.

143
00:07:46,228 --> 00:07:47,394
No, leave them as-is.

144
00:07:47,770 --> 00:07:49,686
I want us to give Yuuji the time

145
00:07:49,770 --> 00:07:53,895
to regain the minimum power
before he gets targeted again.

146
00:07:53,978 --> 00:07:55,579
And so, I need you
to just leave him listed

147
00:07:55,603 --> 00:07:58,353
as deceased on the records.

148
00:07:58,436 --> 00:07:59,311
Ah.

149
00:07:59,394 --> 00:08:01,895
So, you're gonna keep
Itadori hidden away?

150
00:08:01,978 --> 00:08:03,019
No.

151
00:08:03,102 --> 00:08:04,496
I'll have him back in time
for the Exchange Event.

152
00:08:04,520 --> 00:08:05,437
[Shouko] Why?

153
00:08:05,520 --> 00:08:07,687
The reason is simple.

154
00:08:07,771 --> 00:08:09,580
No one can be allowed
to take the events of youth

155
00:08:09,604 --> 00:08:12,687
away from the young
people they're designed for.

156
00:08:12,771 --> 00:08:14,979
I bet this'll shock em!

157
00:08:15,646 --> 00:08:16,646
Not anyone.

158
00:08:24,562 --> 00:08:26,562
I've gotta get outta
here, right now!

159
00:08:27,562 --> 00:08:28,747
I've always had a strong
sense of responsibility,

160
00:08:28,771 --> 00:08:31,270
and I've been saving all my pay

161
00:08:31,354 --> 00:08:33,896
so I can send my four
younger sisters to college, too!

162
00:08:33,979 --> 00:08:36,270
But even I can't fight
my survival instinct!

163
00:08:36,354 --> 00:08:38,730
And I know if I go
near that table, I'll die!

164
00:08:38,813 --> 00:08:41,271
[Jougo] Satoru Gojou!

165
00:08:41,355 --> 00:08:44,480
I wonder, could we kill
him if we joined forces?

166
00:08:44,563 --> 00:08:47,939
No, he'd either flutter
out of your grasp

167
00:08:48,021 --> 00:08:50,563
or, in the worst case,
you'd all get exorcised.

168
00:08:50,647 --> 00:08:52,623
I would recommend you pour
your energy into sealing him

169
00:08:52,647 --> 00:08:55,104
rather than killing him.

170
00:08:55,188 --> 00:08:56,104
How?

171
00:08:56,188 --> 00:08:57,438
Do you have a lead?

172
00:08:58,730 --> 00:09:01,813
We'll use the special-grade
cursed object Prison Realm.

173
00:09:02,772 --> 00:09:03,813
Prison Realm?

174
00:09:05,021 --> 00:09:06,980
Table five hasn't
ordered anything.

175
00:09:07,063 --> 00:09:07,772
I'll go and hurry him up.

176
00:09:07,855 --> 00:09:10,230
He's taking up a whole table.

177
00:09:11,064 --> 00:09:12,898
I'm sorry boss, but I quit!

178
00:09:13,898 --> 00:09:14,814
Huh?

179
00:09:14,898 --> 00:09:17,147
Hey, you come back here!

180
00:09:17,231 --> 00:09:17,648
Prison Realm?

181
00:09:17,731 --> 00:09:18,731
That horrible thing?

182
00:09:20,898 --> 00:09:22,147
It's warm.

183
00:09:22,231 --> 00:09:24,147
The AC quit working?

184
00:09:24,231 --> 00:09:26,606
Relax, Jougo, or you'll
overheat the place.

185
00:09:28,022 --> 00:09:29,314
How are you, sir?

186
00:09:29,397 --> 00:09:30,648
Have you decided on...

187
00:09:33,064 --> 00:09:34,105
Aagh!

188
00:09:35,606 --> 00:09:38,314
(terror scream)

189
00:09:38,397 --> 00:09:40,981
I wish you wouldn't cause
such a commotion, Jougo.

190
00:09:41,064 --> 00:09:42,689
Oh this is nothing.

191
00:09:44,565 --> 00:09:45,482
(horror scream)

192
00:09:45,565 --> 00:09:46,482
What?

193
00:09:46,565 --> 00:09:49,148
(horror scream)

194
00:09:53,649 --> 00:09:55,565
(coughs)

195
00:09:55,649 --> 00:09:58,398
Glad we didn't
choose finer dining.

196
00:09:58,482 --> 00:10:00,857
(panicking)

197
00:10:05,899 --> 00:10:07,732
Tell me, Getou.

198
00:10:07,815 --> 00:10:11,649
How strong am I in
terms of Sukuna's fingers?

199
00:10:11,732 --> 00:10:13,815
[Getou] As a
conservative estimate?

200
00:10:13,899 --> 00:10:15,482
I'd say eight or nine fingers.

201
00:10:15,565 --> 00:10:16,482
Yeah?

202
00:10:16,565 --> 00:10:17,483
That's plenty!

203
00:10:17,566 --> 00:10:18,650
Give me the Prison Realm!

204
00:10:18,733 --> 00:10:20,858
I'll add it to my collection!

205
00:10:20,942 --> 00:10:23,066
And in return I'll promise you,

206
00:10:23,900 --> 00:10:25,316
I'll kill Gojou.

207
00:10:25,775 --> 00:10:31,524
Help!

208
00:10:34,149 --> 00:10:37,900
(melodious electronic music)

209
00:10:39,691 --> 00:10:43,316
(upbeat electronic music)

210
00:10:46,149 --> 00:10:48,024
By the time we
arrived on the scene,

211
00:10:48,107 --> 00:10:50,066
your son was already dead.

212
00:10:50,149 --> 00:10:51,692
I'm sorry.

213
00:10:51,776 --> 00:10:52,943
To be honest,

214
00:10:53,025 --> 00:10:55,651
I was skeptical about saving
any of the people in there.

215
00:10:57,317 --> 00:10:59,525
However, my
friend was different.

216
00:11:01,317 --> 00:11:02,484
He wasn't successful,

217
00:11:02,567 --> 00:11:05,234
but after we confirmed
your son's death

218
00:11:05,317 --> 00:11:07,943
you know he's tried to
bring his body back for you.

219
00:11:09,192 --> 00:11:10,234
It's okay.

220
00:11:14,734 --> 00:11:16,234
"Okazaki Tadashi"

221
00:11:19,901 --> 00:11:20,901
(sigh)

222
00:11:20,984 --> 00:11:21,984
Please take this.

223
00:11:26,401 --> 00:11:27,401
I know it's not much.

224
00:11:28,902 --> 00:11:30,985
I'm sorry we weren't
able to save Tadashi.

225
00:11:32,818 --> 00:11:34,318
It's all right

226
00:11:34,401 --> 00:11:35,735
Don't apologize.

227
00:11:35,818 --> 00:11:37,944
I'm the only one
who will mourn him!

228
00:11:39,193 --> 00:11:40,273
No one else will even care.

229
00:11:40,735 --> 00:11:43,735
(sobbing)

230
00:11:47,652 --> 00:11:50,318
(intense running efforts)

231
00:11:50,401 --> 00:11:51,985
Yo, you're late, Megumi.

232
00:11:52,068 --> 00:11:53,318
Kelp.

233
00:11:53,401 --> 00:11:54,318
Where have you been?

234
00:11:54,401 --> 00:11:56,026
And what does it matter to you?

235
00:11:57,193 --> 00:11:58,778
Answer me something.

236
00:11:58,861 --> 00:11:59,986
Hm?

237
00:12:00,069 --> 00:12:02,736
As a sorcerer, what kind of
people do you want to save?

238
00:12:02,819 --> 00:12:03,694
Huh?

239
00:12:03,778 --> 00:12:05,611
What difference
should it make to me

240
00:12:05,694 --> 00:12:07,319
whether my actions
save anyone at all?

241
00:12:07,402 --> 00:12:08,986
I knew I shouldn't
have asked you.

242
00:12:09,069 --> 00:12:09,986
Say what?

243
00:12:10,069 --> 00:12:11,069
Fushiguro!

244
00:12:12,194 --> 00:12:13,587
Quit asking interview
prep questions

245
00:12:13,611 --> 00:12:15,361
and come switch places with me!

246
00:12:15,444 --> 00:12:17,694
I am so totally sick of
these school uniforms!

247
00:12:17,778 --> 00:12:20,319
Let me go buy some cute
tracksuits for this event!

248
00:12:20,402 --> 00:12:23,361
And here we go.

249
00:12:23,444 --> 00:12:24,444
(yelling)

250
00:12:24,486 --> 00:12:25,986
What the hell are they doing?

251
00:12:26,069 --> 00:12:27,486
Falling practice.

252
00:12:27,569 --> 00:12:28,402
Mustard leaf.

253
00:12:28,486 --> 00:12:30,819
You're both pretty
weak in close quarters.

254
00:12:30,903 --> 00:12:31,904
So first.

255
00:12:33,987 --> 00:12:36,153
See if you can
land a blow on us.

256
00:12:36,237 --> 00:12:37,237
Do that and we'll talk.

257
00:12:38,070 --> 00:12:40,570
You're already a
head above the rest

258
00:12:40,654 --> 00:12:42,820
when it comes to
close combat, Yuuji.

259
00:12:42,904 --> 00:12:45,362
So what you need
to learn to do next is

260
00:12:45,445 --> 00:12:46,820
control cursed energy.

261
00:12:46,904 --> 00:12:50,195
And we need to add to your
basic knowledge of jujutsu.

262
00:12:50,278 --> 00:12:51,570
"Smile"

263
00:12:51,654 --> 00:12:51,862
What's wrong?

264
00:12:51,946 --> 00:12:52,862
Sorry.

265
00:12:52,946 --> 00:12:55,820
I'm just happy 'cause
I know you're the best

266
00:12:55,904 --> 00:12:58,445
and you're the one I
wanted to have train me.

267
00:12:58,862 --> 00:13:02,237
Before, I was too weak
and I couldn't save anybody.

268
00:13:03,487 --> 00:13:05,905
Worse, I nearly
got Fushiguro killed.

269
00:13:06,821 --> 00:13:08,947
I won't be able to face
them the way I am now.

270
00:13:11,112 --> 00:13:12,154
Make me strong.

271
00:13:14,947 --> 00:13:16,027
Make me into the strongest!

272
00:13:19,112 --> 00:13:20,029
(chuckles)

273
00:13:20,112 --> 00:13:22,947
You've got a keen eye.

274
00:13:23,029 --> 00:13:25,780
Well actually, you already
told me you were the strongest.

275
00:13:25,863 --> 00:13:28,404
All right, well
first take a look

276
00:13:28,488 --> 00:13:30,363
at those two soda
cans over there.

277
00:13:34,112 --> 00:13:35,696
Whoa!

278
00:13:35,780 --> 00:13:37,088
[Gojou] This is
with cursed energy,

279
00:13:37,112 --> 00:13:39,405
and that's cursed technique.

280
00:13:39,489 --> 00:13:40,405
I see.

281
00:13:40,489 --> 00:13:41,405
No I don't.

282
00:13:41,489 --> 00:13:42,489
Uhh, okay.

283
00:13:43,948 --> 00:13:45,822
Then think of cursed
energy as electricity,

284
00:13:45,906 --> 00:13:49,489
and cursed technique
as electrical appliances.

285
00:13:49,572 --> 00:13:52,239
Electricity by itself
is hard to use, right?

286
00:13:52,322 --> 00:13:54,822
That's why we run that
electricity through appliances

287
00:13:54,906 --> 00:13:57,447
to achieve various results.

288
00:13:57,530 --> 00:13:59,131
Here, I just fired off
pure cursed energy.

289
00:13:59,155 --> 00:14:00,822
Whereas here, I
channeled cursed energy

290
00:14:00,906 --> 00:14:03,697
into a cursed
technique to activate it,

291
00:14:03,781 --> 00:14:05,572
twisting the can with jujutsu.

292
00:14:06,489 --> 00:14:07,614
Alright!

293
00:14:07,697 --> 00:14:10,239
So I get to learn a really good
cursed technique now huh?

294
00:14:10,322 --> 00:14:11,239
[Gojou] No.

295
00:14:11,323 --> 00:14:11,907
You can't use cursed techniques.

296
00:14:11,990 --> 00:14:12,990
Huh?

297
00:14:14,990 --> 00:14:17,007
Aside from simple Shikigami
and your basic barriers,

298
00:14:17,031 --> 00:14:18,949
cursed techniques
are fundamentally

299
00:14:19,031 --> 00:14:22,281
etched into your body
from the day you're born.

300
00:14:22,365 --> 00:14:23,448
Huh?

301
00:14:23,531 --> 00:14:25,114
So the power of
a jujutsu sorcerer

302
00:14:25,198 --> 00:14:27,657
is about 80% innate talent.

303
00:14:27,740 --> 00:14:30,073
(dazed)

304
00:14:30,156 --> 00:14:31,073
You okay?

305
00:14:31,156 --> 00:14:32,240
Yeah.

306
00:14:32,323 --> 00:14:34,907
I just thought I'd be able
to pull off thunder or fire

307
00:14:35,031 --> 00:14:36,657
or a power bomb or something.

308
00:14:36,740 --> 00:14:39,114
You can do a power
bomb just like Ohnita.

309
00:14:39,198 --> 00:14:39,865
Aww!

310
00:14:39,949 --> 00:14:41,865
This sucks big time!

311
00:14:41,949 --> 00:14:45,074
I wanted to pull off a
Spirit Gun or a Bankai

312
00:14:45,157 --> 00:14:46,574
or a Rasengan or a Dodon Ray!

313
00:14:46,658 --> 00:14:48,338
-What a drag!
-You just can't use them yet!

314
00:14:48,407 --> 00:14:50,324
But eventually, Sukuna's
cursed techniques

315
00:14:50,407 --> 00:14:51,157
will be engraved into your body!

316
00:14:51,241 --> 00:14:53,532
I wanted to fire
off a Kamehameha!

317
00:14:53,616 --> 00:14:55,491
Let's just ignore the
things you can't do

318
00:14:55,574 --> 00:14:57,032
and work on enhancing
your strengths.

319
00:14:57,115 --> 00:14:59,050
We will imbue your fighting
style with cursed energy!

320
00:14:59,074 --> 00:15:02,157
I'm way more scared of
someone with solid basics

321
00:15:02,241 --> 00:15:04,282
than I am of inferior jujutsu.

322
00:15:04,366 --> 00:15:06,282
Like I said your
talent for close combat

323
00:15:06,366 --> 00:15:06,950
is already top-notch.

324
00:15:07,032 --> 00:15:09,032
(sudden realization gasp)

325
00:15:09,115 --> 00:15:10,115
But wait a sec!

326
00:15:10,157 --> 00:15:10,950
I already know how to do that!

327
00:15:11,032 --> 00:15:13,324
Get up.

328
00:15:13,407 --> 00:15:16,866
Against that special-grade,
I got it to work, somehow.

329
00:15:19,075 --> 00:15:21,742
Then give it a try.

330
00:15:21,825 --> 00:15:22,825
Hit me here.

331
00:15:22,909 --> 00:15:24,825
Not that I think you can.

332
00:15:24,909 --> 00:15:26,575
Don't blame me if you get hurt.

333
00:15:26,659 --> 00:15:28,075
Come one, hurry up, try it.

334
00:15:32,784 --> 00:15:35,158
That punch had
zero cursed energy.

335
00:15:35,242 --> 00:15:36,533
But why?

336
00:15:36,617 --> 00:15:38,825
Cause it requires
negative emotions.

337
00:15:38,909 --> 00:15:40,367
In the fight that
you're recalling,

338
00:15:40,450 --> 00:15:43,116
you were probably brimming
with fear and with anger.

339
00:15:43,200 --> 00:15:44,200
Ah!

340
00:15:44,283 --> 00:15:46,075
So you have to
constantly be flipping out

341
00:15:46,158 --> 00:15:48,242
in order to use
your cursed energy?

342
00:15:48,325 --> 00:15:49,825
But now that you mention it

343
00:15:49,909 --> 00:15:51,576
Fushiguro's always ticked off.

344
00:15:51,660 --> 00:15:51,910
Demon Dogs!

345
00:15:51,993 --> 00:15:54,034
(barks)

346
00:15:54,117 --> 00:15:55,117
Not quite.

347
00:15:57,618 --> 00:15:58,534
What's wrong?

348
00:15:58,618 --> 00:16:00,117
I'm irritated all of a sudden.

349
00:16:00,201 --> 00:16:01,302
-Huh?
-No, I don't mean with you.

350
00:16:01,326 --> 00:16:04,368
-[Toge] Salmon roe.
-Only a month and a half left.

351
00:16:04,451 --> 00:16:05,451
So no daydreaming!

352
00:16:05,493 --> 00:16:07,826
Now here, try your
hand at the long one next.

353
00:16:10,034 --> 00:16:12,660
This actually feels pretty good.

354
00:16:14,243 --> 00:16:16,409
All students are trained
to produce cursed energy

355
00:16:16,493 --> 00:16:18,133
using even the faintest
sparks of emotion.

356
00:16:18,159 --> 00:16:20,117
And they're trained in ways

357
00:16:20,201 --> 00:16:21,260
to avoid wasting
their cursed energy

358
00:16:21,284 --> 00:16:24,117
when their emotions
are flaring up as well.

359
00:16:25,202 --> 00:16:26,619
(dismayed gasp)

360
00:16:26,702 --> 00:16:28,744
There are several
training methods for this.

361
00:16:28,827 --> 00:16:32,035
The one I'm going to use on
you is especially exhausting.

362
00:16:32,118 --> 00:16:33,118
Okay, what's that?

363
00:16:33,160 --> 00:16:35,827
Watching movies!

364
00:16:35,911 --> 00:16:37,202
Watching movies?

365
00:16:37,285 --> 00:16:39,118
Yup!

366
00:16:39,202 --> 00:16:39,953
From classics to
C-grade horror movies

367
00:16:40,035 --> 00:16:42,285
to terrible French movies.

368
00:16:42,369 --> 00:16:44,661
Nonstop as long as
you can stay awake.

369
00:16:44,744 --> 00:16:47,202
Of course you won't be
watching them all alone.

370
00:16:47,285 --> 00:16:49,244
(snoring)

371
00:16:49,327 --> 00:16:51,118
You'll be watching
them with this guy.

372
00:16:51,202 --> 00:16:54,285
[Yuuji] What's with the
cute-but-creepy doll?

373
00:16:54,369 --> 00:16:54,994
It's cute?

374
00:16:55,077 --> 00:16:57,619
It's another cursed corpse.

375
00:16:57,702 --> 00:16:58,620
From the Principal!

376
00:16:58,703 --> 00:17:00,745
Yeah, I recognize his style.

377
00:17:05,995 --> 00:17:08,620
But, I'm not seeing
the point here.

378
00:17:08,703 --> 00:17:09,912
Don't be hasty, now.

379
00:17:09,995 --> 00:17:10,995
You'll see soon enough.

380
00:17:13,161 --> 00:17:14,620
That cursed corpse will wake up

381
00:17:14,703 --> 00:17:16,245
and attack you just like that,

382
00:17:16,328 --> 00:17:18,787
if you don't keep cursed
energy flowing into it.

383
00:17:21,495 --> 00:17:22,662
Like I said before,

384
00:17:22,745 --> 00:17:24,221
we've got all kinds of
movies here to choose from.

385
00:17:24,245 --> 00:17:27,495
Tear-jerkers,
thrillers, comedies.

386
00:17:27,578 --> 00:17:30,620
Movies to make you laugh
or cry or gross you out.

387
00:17:31,536 --> 00:17:33,329
Your first assignment
is to watch an movie

388
00:17:33,412 --> 00:17:36,120
from start to finish, without
waking the cursed corpse.

389
00:17:36,204 --> 00:17:39,246
This trains you to maintain a
steady output of cursed energy

390
00:17:39,329 --> 00:17:41,329
no matter what
emotions you feel.

391
00:17:41,412 --> 00:17:43,412
You can't use too
much or too little.

392
00:17:44,329 --> 00:17:47,120
(aggravated flailing)

393
00:17:47,204 --> 00:17:48,496
(relieved sigh)

394
00:17:48,579 --> 00:17:51,663
For now I have it set to the
faint level of cursed energy

395
00:17:51,746 --> 00:17:52,663
that you're able to produce.

396
00:17:52,746 --> 00:17:55,496
But soon it'll start
demanding greater output,

397
00:17:55,579 --> 00:17:57,871
so you can't let
your guard down.

398
00:17:57,955 --> 00:18:00,371
I couldn't let it down
even if I wanted to.

399
00:18:00,454 --> 00:18:01,955
Where do you want to start?

400
00:18:02,037 --> 00:18:03,329
I recommend this one.

401
00:18:03,412 --> 00:18:06,247
The heroine's annoying but
she dies gloriously in the end.

402
00:18:06,330 --> 00:18:07,080
Thanks for the spoiler.

403
00:18:07,163 --> 00:18:08,205
Hey, I know!

404
00:18:08,288 --> 00:18:10,789
Let's start with an action ad...

405
00:18:11,789 --> 00:18:13,121
Oh, come on!

406
00:18:13,205 --> 00:18:14,080
Hey!

407
00:18:14,163 --> 00:18:16,372
Keep that cursed energy steady!

408
00:18:17,997 --> 00:18:19,580
Carrying cursed tools, huh?

409
00:18:21,080 --> 00:18:23,139
I'm fine with supplementing
close combat with weapons,

410
00:18:23,163 --> 00:18:25,163
but with my cursed technique

411
00:18:25,247 --> 00:18:27,705
I want to be able to
have my hands free.

412
00:18:27,789 --> 00:18:30,330
Swords cost you time
sheathing and unsheathing them.

413
00:18:30,413 --> 00:18:33,080
So Zenin, you often carry around

414
00:18:33,163 --> 00:18:35,330
two or even more
around with you don't you?

415
00:18:35,413 --> 00:18:36,538
How do you do that?

416
00:18:36,622 --> 00:18:38,497
Oh I make Panda carry them.

417
00:18:38,580 --> 00:18:40,790
I knew I shouldn't
have asked, part two.

418
00:18:40,873 --> 00:18:43,164
Some jujutsu sorcerers
keep cursed spirits

419
00:18:43,248 --> 00:18:44,265
that can store and
retrieve objects.

420
00:18:44,289 --> 00:18:47,790
Yeah, but he can't do
that, it's a rare ability.

421
00:18:47,873 --> 00:18:49,748
And it takes time
to tame them, too.

422
00:18:49,831 --> 00:18:51,915
But if you do find
any, let me know.

423
00:18:51,998 --> 00:18:54,206
[Panda] It'll cost you a
year's supply of Calpas.

424
00:18:55,498 --> 00:18:58,248
But there's just,
one thing I don't get.

425
00:18:59,831 --> 00:19:01,206
Why did you run?

426
00:19:01,289 --> 00:19:04,581
Kind of a waste of your talents.

427
00:19:04,665 --> 00:19:07,248
Do I have the potential
to beat special-grades?

428
00:19:08,831 --> 00:19:10,456
Is that what he meant by that?

429
00:19:16,457 --> 00:19:17,457
Tuna, tuna.

430
00:19:17,499 --> 00:19:18,415
Huh?

431
00:19:18,499 --> 00:19:19,499
What's that?

432
00:19:20,290 --> 00:19:21,290
Zen'in?

433
00:19:22,999 --> 00:19:24,874
I think I know how to do it.

434
00:19:29,666 --> 00:19:30,582
Ura-Hara?

435
00:19:30,666 --> 00:19:31,666
Where's Ura-Hara?

436
00:19:31,707 --> 00:19:32,749
Am I lost?

437
00:19:35,040 --> 00:19:37,249
Do I cut the red
wire or the blue one?

438
00:19:37,332 --> 00:19:38,499
I need to know!

439
00:19:40,165 --> 00:19:41,958
In the area where I used to live

440
00:19:42,040 --> 00:19:43,200
we had designated trash bags.

441
00:19:43,249 --> 00:19:45,415
What are you talking about?

442
00:19:45,500 --> 00:19:46,792
We're running out of time!

443
00:19:46,875 --> 00:19:48,792
And the bags
were red for plastic

444
00:19:48,875 --> 00:19:50,792
and blue for combustible trash.

445
00:19:50,875 --> 00:19:52,309
I thought, shouldn't
it be the opposite?

446
00:19:52,333 --> 00:19:53,250
It should be red!

447
00:19:53,333 --> 00:19:55,667
Anyone would go with red!

448
00:19:56,708 --> 00:19:58,250
Alright, I'll trust you.

449
00:20:00,375 --> 00:20:03,375
(anxious breathing)

450
00:20:09,750 --> 00:20:10,875
Ugh!

451
00:20:10,959 --> 00:20:13,291
(boxing bell ringing)

452
00:20:13,375 --> 00:20:14,208
(coughs)

453
00:20:14,291 --> 00:20:17,291
Don't attack me while
I'm drinking soda!

454
00:20:17,375 --> 00:20:18,833
Don't drink.

455
00:20:18,918 --> 00:20:20,393
But you can't watch a
movie without chips and soda!

456
00:20:20,417 --> 00:20:22,584
You have a point there.

457
00:20:24,001 --> 00:20:26,209
Well, Gojou's got to get going.

458
00:20:26,292 --> 00:20:27,876
So just keep hanging in there.

459
00:20:27,960 --> 00:20:30,501
Is this really gonna
make me stronger?

460
00:20:30,584 --> 00:20:33,292
(chuckles)

461
00:20:33,376 --> 00:20:34,376
Oh, yeah.

462
00:20:35,376 --> 00:20:37,334
While you were dead,
did you talk to Sukuna?

463
00:20:37,417 --> 00:20:38,417
Not sure.

464
00:20:39,542 --> 00:20:41,334
And before he
repaired your heart,

465
00:20:41,417 --> 00:20:44,292
did he suggest any
deals or make conditions?

466
00:20:44,376 --> 00:20:46,376
Ohh!

467
00:20:46,459 --> 00:20:48,376
I think he did say
something like that.

468
00:20:49,709 --> 00:20:51,542
But I can't remember
what it was.

469
00:20:52,961 --> 00:20:54,002
I see.

470
00:20:59,252 --> 00:21:00,877
We have some time
before your appointment

471
00:21:00,961 --> 00:21:01,877
with the principal.

472
00:21:01,961 --> 00:21:03,502
Do you want to stop anywhere?

473
00:21:03,585 --> 00:21:04,877
No thanks.

474
00:21:04,961 --> 00:21:07,293
I'll surprise him and
show up early for a change.

475
00:21:10,961 --> 00:21:11,877
Stop here.

476
00:21:11,961 --> 00:21:12,961
[Ijichi] Huh?

477
00:21:13,043 --> 00:21:13,377
Right here?

478
00:21:13,460 --> 00:21:14,377
You go on ahead.

479
00:21:14,460 --> 00:21:16,543
[Ijichi] Agh!

480
00:21:16,627 --> 00:21:18,085
Is this a test or something?

481
00:21:18,168 --> 00:21:18,961
You're going to hit me

482
00:21:19,043 --> 00:21:20,311
if I drive away without
you, aren't you?

483
00:21:20,335 --> 00:21:23,543
Just what type of
guy do you think I am?

484
00:21:23,627 --> 00:21:24,627
[Ijichi] Okay then.

485
00:21:32,836 --> 00:21:33,878
All right.

486
00:21:34,795 --> 00:21:37,878
(banshee attack wail)

487
00:21:39,003 --> 00:21:41,753
(menacing laugh)

488
00:21:41,836 --> 00:21:43,127
I see.

489
00:21:43,211 --> 00:21:44,253
Who are you then?

490
00:21:45,544 --> 00:21:50,294
("Lost in Paradise"
by ALI feat. AKLO)

491
00:23:15,339 --> 00:23:16,506
[s] Juju Stroll!

492
00:23:19,381 --> 00:23:21,464
[] It's Satoru
Gojou's Go Go Gojou!

493
00:23:21,547 --> 00:23:24,047
We are here at my alma mater,

494
00:23:24,130 --> 00:23:26,631
Tokyo Metropolitan
Jujutsu Tech High School.

495
00:23:26,714 --> 00:23:27,839
Oh no!

496
00:23:27,923 --> 00:23:29,464
A boy in trouble already?

497
00:23:29,547 --> 00:23:32,839
He's a new student, having
trouble producing cursed energy!

498
00:23:32,923 --> 00:23:34,422
Let's try to help him!

499
00:23:34,506 --> 00:23:37,839
Imagine yourself on a
narrow pathway at school.

500
00:23:37,923 --> 00:23:40,131
Standing before you
is a row of college boys,

501
00:23:40,215 --> 00:23:42,048
and you can see they
haven't noticed you.

502
00:23:42,131 --> 00:23:43,507
You want to kill them all!

503
00:23:43,590 --> 00:23:44,507
And so you--

504
00:23:44,590 --> 00:23:45,590
Shut up.

505
00:23:46,465 --> 00:23:50,507
(tense music)

506
00:23:52,131 --> 00:23:53,757
"Episode 7: Assault"

